@startuml
title COLORS Web Application - Conceptual Class Diagram
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
left to right direction

class "User" as User <<database entity>> {
  +ID : integer
  +firstName : string
  +lastName : string
  +Login : string
  +Password : string
}

class "Color" as Color <<database entity>> {
  +UserId : integer
  +Name : string
}

class "Colors Web App" as WebApp <<JavaScript functions>> {
  -userId : integer
  -firstName : string
  -lastName : string
  +doLogin()
  +saveCookie()
  +readCookie()
  +doLogout()
  +addColor()
  +searchColor()
}

class "Login.php" as LoginAPI <<PHP API>> {
  +getRequestInfo()
  +returnWithInfo(firstName, lastName, id)
  +returnWithError(error)
}
class "AddColor.php" as AddAPI <<PHP API>> {
  +getRequestInfo()
  +returnWithError(error)
}
class "SearchColors.php" as SearchAPI <<PHP API>> {
  +getRequestInfo()
  +returnWithInfo(searchResults)
  +returnWithError(error)
}

User "1" -- "0..*" Color : owns (via UserId)
WebApp ..> LoginAPI : login credentials
WebApp ..> AddAPI : color + userId
WebApp ..> SearchAPI : search + userId
LoginAPI ..> User : queries Users table
AddAPI ..> Color : inserts into Colors
SearchAPI ..> Color : searches Colors

note bottom of User
  User and Color represent database records.
  PHP and JavaScript files are procedural,
  shown as conceptual UML classifiers.
  The SQL schema was not supplied;
  column types and ownership multiplicity
  are inferred from the code.
end note
@enduml
